  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Which of the following functions has the domain $Z?$\n\n- $p:Z\\to [0,3]$\n- $q:(0,7)\\to Z$\n- $r:{Z}^{+}\\to Z$",
  "worked_solution": "The notation $f:X\\to Y$ means that the function $f$ maps the set $X$ to the set $Y.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $X,$\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $Y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our functions.\n\n- The domain of $p$ is $Z,$ the set of integers.\n\n- The domain of $q$ is $(0,7),$ the interval from $0$ to $7$ (excluding $0$ and $7$).\n\n- The domain of $r$ is ${Z}^{+},$ the set of positive integers.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
